/-!
# Stacks Tag 0B5H over an algebraically closed field

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] — a field `k` and a proper one-dimensional `k`-scheme `X` with
`H⁰(X, 𝒪_X) = k` — let `ω_X = H^{-1}(f^×(𝒪_{Spec k}))` be the dualizing sheaf of
[Stacks, Tag 0BS2] and let `ℒ` be a very ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module of degree at least two.
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] asserts that `ω_X ⊗ ℒ` is generated by its global sections. This file proves
it over an algebraically closed base field, which is the case the source proves directly; the
general case is reduced to this one in `DualizingTwistGenerationAnyField.lean`.

## Main results

* `epi_globalSectionsHom_comp_of_coherent`: [Stacks, Tag 0B5F] with its hypothesis on
  submodules of `ℱ` asked of coherent submodules only, which is what the source states and what
  its proof uses.
* `epi_globalSectionsHom_of_forall_isClosed_of_coherent`: global generation of `ℱ` for an
  extension of a module with zero-dimensional support by a module `ω` with first-cohomology
  duality, from a section of `ℒ` vanishing at each closed point.
* `noCoherentSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport_tensorSheaf`: `ω ⊗ ℒ` has no nonzero coherent
  submodule supported in dimension zero, from clause (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2] for `ω`.
* `nonempty_generatingSections_dualizing_tensorSheaf_of_isAlgClosed_coherent`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] over an algebraically closed field.**

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.NoSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.VanishingSectionData` of
`DualizingTwistGeneration.lean` quantify over *all* submodules of `ℱ`, and the second also asks
for the vanishing of `H¹` on every submodule of `𝒬`. At the canonical dualizing sheaf only
coherent submodules are controlled (clause (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2] is about quasi-coherent
modules), and that is all the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0B5F] applies its hypothesis to: the one
submodule it is applied to is a quotient of a coherent module. The coherent forms are therefore
stated here under new names, `NoCoherentSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport` and
`CoherentVanishingSectionData`.

The tensor product is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor`, written out in the statements
as in the other files of this directory.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5F)
